{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011Cfbcu4vvKqEd3ooyTfPNm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe three new units are well-placed: the checked exception, its escalation handler, and the check function each sit in the right package, follow the one-public-method convention (`service`, matching `ValidateOwner`), and are wired coherently between `validate` and `build`. The only structural issue is duplicated normalization.\n\n**Finding — telephone normalization rule is duplicated, with no single source of truth**\n\nThe \"normalize to digits\" rule now exists in two places:\n- `ValidateOwner.java:48` — `request.getTelephone().replaceAll(\"\\\\D\", \"\")`\n- `CheckOwnerTelephoneUnique.java:29` — `value.replaceAll(\"\\\\D\", \"\")` (the private `normalize`)\n\n\"Normalized telephone\" is the central concept of this spec, and its definition is copied into two units that must agree. If one changes (e.g. ValidateOwner starts stripping leading country codes, or treats `null` differently), the uniqueness comparison silently diverges from what actually gets stored — exactly the kind of drift a maintainer wouldn't expect across two separate files.\n\nCompounding it: by the time `CheckOwnerTelephoneUnique.service` runs, `ValidateOwner` has already written the ten-digit value back onto the body (`ValidateOwner.java:52`), so `normalize(request.getTelephone())` on the *incoming* side is redundant re-normalization of an already-normalized value — it only looks necessary because the rule was re-implemented rather than reused.\n\nSuggested fix: give the normalization a single home and have both steps call it — e.g. a static helper (`OwnerTelephone.normalize(...)`) or a method on `OwnerFieldsDto`. `CheckOwnerTelephoneUnique` then needs normalization only for the *stored* owner values (whose incidental formatting is the real reason the helper exists); the request side can use `request.getTelephone()` directly since it is already normalized."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1742,"cache_read_input_tokens":25519,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1742},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6368f14c-7fe4-4578-9fce-f5c32700f016","uuid":"8f0871d2-7a98-4d54-9f01-8b41e0c718af","timestamp":"2026-10-01T13:46:37.879Z","request_id":"req_011Cfbcu4aaPUtQL6AhvAoCG"}
